ased at makop  in the caucasus region of today's russia  in other words  the eastern front eric hartman would be  part of the titanic struggle of the axis  versus the soviet union  at jg 52 eric was assigned as a wingman  to sergeant edmund rossman technically  hartmann outranked him but amongst  fighter pilots official ranks meant  little what mattered was experience and  rosman had plenty of wisdom to impart on  the rookie officer rosman suffered from  an old arm injury which made it  impossible for him to perform the  maneuvers typical of a protracted  dogfight the sergeant preferred to stalk  his prey from above evaluating the  situation if an enemy craft did not take  evasive action rosman dove in shooting  at extremely close range harmon later  adopted and perfected this tactic which  he called see decide attack break but on  his first combat mission youthful  impatience prevailed on october the 14th  1942 rosman and hartman spotted 10  soviet planes rosman urged caution but  eric went full throttle and engaged in  enemy fighter it was a debacle not only  did he fail to score a single hit but he  almost collided with the enemy hartmann  then hastily sawed above the clouds to  escape retaliation consuming all of his  fuel with a dry tank all he could do was  crash land and hope for the best he  survived unscathed but his guarding  officer grounded him literally for three  days of hard labor once again he learned  from the experience and started to  listen to rosman's advice this allowed  him to claim his first two victories in  november and december shooting down two  fighter bombers the il-2 stermovics in  early 1943 eric was assigned to a new  mentor captain walter krapinski the  older officer gave hotman the nickname  booby this means young boy and it was  due to his youthful appearance during  missions krapinski would constantly  argon eric to get in the thick of the  action with calls of a booby getting  closer under the captain's guidance  booby's tally i